From 214b6332bf6dc8d68ffc96392cadd00e009dbab6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: frank-energie-mcp scaffold <dev@example.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 19:37:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Implement first-milestone MCP server

Adds the src/ layout and price/account tools described in README.md's
'First milestone' and 'Planned structure' sections:

- config.py / auth.py: env-based credentials, lazy login, single
  FrankEnergie client per process
- models.py: deterministic JSON serialization for MarketPrices/Price/
  UserSites, plus ToolError + translate_frank_energie_error() so backend
  exceptions never leak internals to MCP clients (SECURITY.md,
  docs/DEVELOPMENT.md)
- tools/prices.py: get_current_prices, get_today_prices,
  get_tomorrow_prices, get_gas_price (public, no credentials needed)
- tools/account.py: get_account, list_sites (only registered when
  FRANK_USERNAME/FRANK_PASSWORD are set)
- server.py: MCPServer (mcp>=2.0.0) wiring; FastMCP was the v1 name
- docs/API.md: tool reference and error-translation table, following
  the existing docs/DEVELOPMENT.md naming convention
- tests/test_server.py: verifies account tools are absent without
  credentials

All Frank Energie communication stays in python-frank-energie per the
architecture rule in CONTRIBUTING.md / AI_POLICY.md. ruff clean,
pytest passing.
